OpenCapAveMAEPerformanceVals/
BadTrialsFromTrustedDataset/

# ProcessAddbiomechnics/ was listed above as a cohort dataset, but it holds no
# data - only updateModel.py, which ProcessData.py imports for fix_xml_masses
# and knee_coupling_is_canonical_xml. Ignoring it meant a fresh clone hit the
# bare `except Exception` around that import and silently lost mass-fixing and
# knee-coupling validation. Track the source, ignore anything else.
ProcessAddbiomechnics/*
!ProcessAddbiomechnics/*.py

# Same hazard as ProcessAddbiomechnics above: scripts/data_prep/
# generate_noised12_distributed.py imports generate_sine_noise from here, so
# that one module has to be tracked or the script cannot run on a fresh clone.
# The analysis outputs in this directory stay ignored.
!NoiseAndPowerAnalOfInputData/generate_sine_noise.py

